WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.490
Code is cheap. Good decisions aren't.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.649
This page was built in one afternoon.

3
00:00:05.649 --> 00:00:07.385
I didn't type most of the code.

4
00:00:07.385 --> 00:00:09.470
I decided what it needed to be.

5
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.176
It started with a spec.

6
00:00:11.176 --> 00:00:15.311
What's in, what's out, and what has to be true at the end.

7
00:00:15.461 --> 00:00:18.200
Then, AI agents with different roles.

8
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.311
One builds. One writes.

9
00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:23.799
One checks, without knowing how it was made.

10
00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:26.765
Skills teach the agent to work the way I do.

11
00:00:26.765 --> 00:00:29.268
MCP connects it to real systems.

12
00:00:29.418 --> 00:00:33.239
Before going live, an agent opened the page in a browser,

13
00:00:33.239 --> 00:00:36.707
on desktop and mobile, and flagged seven issues.

14
00:00:36.707 --> 00:00:39.056
Only then was it published.

15
00:00:39.206 --> 00:00:42.435
From request to deploy, on the same day.

16
00:00:42.585 --> 00:00:44.956
I'm Lucas Castro, hands-on Tech Lead.

17
00:00:44.956 --> 00:00:46.240
AI writes the code.

18
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.368
The decisions are still mine.
